{title: Zechariah Son of Berechiah}
{subtitle: Zechariah 1:1; Ezra 5:1; Nehemiah 3:4–30; Matthew 23:35}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In the eighth month of the second year of Darius
[G]The word of the LORD came to the prophet Zechariah
[Dm]He was the son of Berechiah
A [C]man of Levitical clan in the ancient [Dm]land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Prophesying to the Jews in Judah and Jerusalem
[G]In the name of the God of Israel who was over them [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Zechariah son of Berechiah
[G]A link in the lineage of the prop[Dm]hets
Between the sanctuary and the altar
His [C]story is told in the scrip[Dm]tures
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He belongs to a Levitical clan
[G]Living after the Babylonian exile
[Dm]His role is a link in the prophetic lineage
Con[C]necting Zechariah to his grandfather Iddo
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Dm]Zechariah son of Berechiah
[G]A link in the lineage of the prop[Dm]hets
Between the sanctuary and the altar
His [C]story is told in the scrip[Dm]tures
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Jesus refers to Zechariah son of Barachiah
[G]Whom you murdered between the sanctuary and the altar
[Dm]All the righteous blood shed on the earth
From [C]Abel to this prophet in the biblical tra[Dm]dition
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Zechariah son of Berechiah
Re[G]membered in the book of Zecha[Dm]riah
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
